<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The tile the stack of paper sits on. The source artwork is transparent, so this is the whole of
      the icon's ground; change it together with assets/icon_mk1.svg rather than instead of it.

      Near-black, warmed onto the app's own hue (350) rather than left a true black, so the tile
      belongs to this app and not to Android.

      This deliberately gives up on the sheets reading against the ground — their dark end is
      #0C0B0B and lands at 1.1:1 here, so the bottom of the stack merges into the tile and what the
      eye gets is the near-white page edges floating, with the sheets implied above them by the
      gradient's lighter top. That is a look rather than a mistake: it is the same one the reference dark
      theme has, and it is why this was chosen over the mid grey that made all three tones legible.

      The cost is that on a black wallpaper the tile has almost no edge of its own — 1.1:1 against a
      #141414 launcher — so the icon reads as a floating mark rather than as a tile. If that ever
      looks broken rather than elegant, the mid grey #9B8C8F is the measured alternative: sheets
      6.1:1 and 2.3:1, edges 2.4:1.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#14100F</color>
</resources>
